post.description:
Accepts a SARIF/SBOM/TEXT/AUDIT report as multipart/form-data and processes it for the given repository.

The `file` part can be either a raw report file or a ZIP archive.

ZIP archive requirements:
- exactly one report file;
- the report file must be in the archive root;
- directories, nested paths, and extra files are rejected;
- the single uncompressed entry must be no larger than 100 MB.

The file content must match `reportType`: SARIF uploads should contain a SARIF report, and SBOM uploads should contain SPDX or CycloneDX JSON. The REST request body is limited to 100 MB.

Create archives without parent directories: `zip report.zip report.sarif`. Do not zip a folder with `zip -r report.zip reports/`, because nested paths are rejected.

Set `isReactive=true` to process in the background — note that it answers 202 before parsing, so a report rejected later is reported only in the logs. Keep the default `isReactive=false` to get 400 with the reason the report was rejected, which is what an AUDIT upload needs: its message names every result and field to fix before uploading the corrected report again.
